= Blockchain =

== Overview ==
'''Blockchain''' is a distributed digital ledger in which validated records are grouped into ordered blocks that are cryptographically linked and replicated across a network according to established consensus rules.

Cryptographic links make past records tamper-evident and, depending on the protocol and adversary assumptions, increasingly difficult to rewrite. Consensus rules determine which proposed state transitions become part of the accepted ledger history.

Blockchains can be permissionless or permissioned and may support payments, general computation, asset registries, identity systems, or other applications. A blockchain is not synonymous with cryptocurrency.

Not every distributed ledger is a blockchain. Other replicated-ledger structures may order or reconcile records without grouping them into a cryptographically linked chain of blocks.

== Boundaries ==
* blockchain ≠ cryptocurrency
* blockchain ≠ every distributed ledger
* tamper-resistant ≠ absolutely immutable

